  Plaintext e1 = first_slot >> 1;
  Plaintext e2 = first_slot >> 2;
  Ciphertext output = coordinates[0] * first_slot;
  output += coordinates[1] * e1;
  output += coordinates[2] * e2;
  output.set_output("output");
}
```

I have no valid improvement left. Attempt 7 showed that `Plaintext` cannot be shifted, so unit masks cannot be built from `first_slot`. Every other packing I tried either mixes the columns or needs constants the CKKS rules do not allow. I am submitting the baseline kernel as my final answer.

